>Design of Physicians&#x02019; Health Study II-A Randomized Trial of Beta-Carotene, Vitamins E and C, and Multivitamins, in Prevention of Cancer, Cardiovascular Disease, and Eye Disease, and Review of Resutls of Completed Trials</article-title><source>Ann. Epidemiol</source><year>2000</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>125</fpage><lpage>134</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10691066</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b7-ijerph-06-00635"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fulton</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Elton</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wood</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Oliver</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cigarette smoking, social class and nutrient intake: relevance to coronary heart disease</article-title><source>Eur. J. Clin. Nutr</source><year>1988</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>797</fpage><lpage>803</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2846266</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8-ijerph-06-00635"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zondervan</surname><given-names>KT</given-names></name><name><surname>Ocke</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Smit</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name><name><surname>Seidell</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Do dietary and supplementary intakes of antioxidants differ with smoking status?</article-title><source>Int. J. Epidemiol</source><year>1996</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>70</fpage><lpage>79</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8666507</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ijerph-06-00635"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group p